# Configure a provider compatible with Chat Completions JSON output. No provider/model/prices are assumed.
ILLOURA_RAP_LLM_ENDPOINT=
ILLOURA_RAP_LLM_MODEL=
ILLOURA_RAP_LLM_API_KEY=
ILLOURA_RAP_LLM_INPUT_USD_PER_MILLION=
ILLOURA_RAP_LLM_OUTPUT_USD_PER_MILLION=
ILLOURA_RAP_LLM_MAX_DOCUMENT_USD=
ILLOURA_RAP_LLM_MAX_BATCH_USD=

# Comma-separated account UUIDs authorised for privacy clearance and document review.
# Resolve each to a named reviewer in the access directory; never put people's names here or in review rows.
ILLOURA_RAP_REVIEWER_IDS=

# Privacy gate: old prepared packages are refused. `prepare --privacy-review PATH` requires a JSON
# object keyed by retained PDF SHA256. Each entry has exactly: pages, licence, privacy_review.
# pages maps PDF page numbers (strings) to exact contiguous, manually checked excerpts.
# Include only procurement text: omit people (including champions, CEO letters and signatures),
# addresses, sole-trader ABNs and contact details. Also check organisation, source URL and copyright.
# privacy_review has exactly reviewer_id (registered account UUID), contains_personal_data (false),
# payload_sha256: rap_extract.digest({organisation,document_sha256,source_url,licence,pages}).
# This is an accountable human attestation, not automatic name detection or a digital signature.
# Selected excerpts must occur verbatim in the retained PDF, whose hash is rechecked before/after calls.
# Preparation never writes raw pages. Quotes can only come from the cleared excerpts; raw provider
# responses, request headers and error bodies are never persisted. Free-text review notes are disabled.
# Review approval is separate: `review --by ACCOUNT_UUID --document-sha256 EXACT_SHA ...`.
# Legacy manual findings are excluded; RAP directory exports also require privacy clearance before reimport.
# Their top-level privacy_review binds digest({records,provenance}) using the same three review fields.
# Batch accounting reserves the conservative request bound, even when reported usage costs less.
# Missing usage stays unknown (NULL cost), stops the batch and blocks repeat requests for unchanged
# document/pages/model/endpoint, including after prompt or budget changes. No paid-call retries.
# Pricing must cover the provider's complete token charges. The estimate bounds UTF-8 input bytes
# plus 4096 overhead and 2500 completion tokens; provider billing remains authoritative.
